From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:38:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 143/143] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=no_quad_merge_block lets
 Metal merge triangles into quads

Why the block exists: Apple GPUs merge adjacent triangles of a draw
into shared 2x2 quads, so a quad on the seam of two triangles is shaded
with real fragments of both rather than helper invocations of one, and
its derivatives (an implicit-LOD sample's mip level) mix two
interpolation functions. Under perspective that gives wrong mip levels
along the seam, which the CTS's projected-geometry sampling tests
check per pixel (KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Portability#54, the
samplingImplicitLODProjectedGeometryAccuracyConformance capability
MoltenVK reports as not supported). KosmicKrisp keeps Vulkan's per-
triangle quads instead: for any fragment shader that needs full or
coarse quad helper invocations, kk_lower_fs (kk_shader.c) runs
msl_disable_triangle_merge (msl_nir_lower_common.c), which reads
[[barycentric_coord]] and stores zero colour when all three weights
are negative, a condition that never holds but that the MSL compiler
cannot drop, so Metal stops merging; a shader with no colour output
writes the sample mask instead, which upstream's comment says costs
more. It is skipped only for multisampled pipelines on Apple7/8 before
OS 27, where a sample mask write broke derivatives. It is not an OS 26
workaround and has no switch. The mesa tree here is a shallow copy of
the pin, so the commit that added it was not read; the reason is the
code's own comments and the issue.

The cost is per fragment shader that samples with implicit LOD: 550 of
RDR2's 584 fragment shaders have it. Each pays an extra interpolant and
three compares and selects, and above all loses quad merging, so small
triangles (foliage, hair, distant geometry) shade more partly covered
quads and helper lanes. DXMT, which D3D titles run correctly on, does
not block merging.

With the flag the pass is not run: fragment shaders are as Metal would
build them without the block, and derivatives along a triangle seam
may differ from Vulkan's (no D3D title is known to depend on it). The
flag is in the pipeline cache UUID with the other MSL-changing
switches, so the disk cache and application pipeline caches never mix
MSL built with and without it, and in 0118's must-be-named set
(MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=all alone does not turn it on). Without it every
shader, and the UUID, are as before.

Linear: PLA-541
Class: feature
Evidence: $PLAYPORT_BUILD/agent-notes/pla541/kk-compiler.md (finding 3,
 the 550 of 584 RDR2 fragment shaders)
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.c           | 4 +++-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.h           | 7 +++++++
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 2 +-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c          | 6 +++++-
 4 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.c
index bdda253..655cf52 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.c
@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@ const struct debug_named_value experimental_flags[] = {
    {"cmd_bo_classes", KK_EXPERIMENTAL_CMD_BO_CLASSES},
    {"private_memory", KK_EXPERIMENTAL_PRIVATE_MEMORY},
    {"barrier_device_vis", KK_EXPERIMENTAL_BARRIER_DEVICE_VIS},
+   {"no_quad_merge_block", KK_EXPERIMENTAL_NO_QUAD_MERGE_BLOCK},
    {NULL, 0},
 };
 
@@ -135,7 +136,8 @@ kk_process_debug_variable(void)
       KK_EXPERIMENTAL_NO_FP_PRESERVE | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_FP_PRECISE_ONLY |
       KK_EXPERIMENTAL_UBO_UNBOUNDED | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_NARROW_BARRIERS |
       KK_EXPERIMENTAL_DS_DONT_CARE | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_CMD_RETIRE |
-      KK_EXPERIMENTAL_PRIVATE_MEMORY | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_BARRIER_DEVICE_VIS;
+      KK_EXPERIMENTAL_PRIVATE_MEMORY | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_BARRIER_DEVICE_VIS |
+      KK_EXPERIMENTAL_NO_QUAD_MERGE_BLOCK;
    for (const struct debug_named_value *f = experimental_flags; f->name; f++) {
       if (f->value != UINT64_MAX && (f->value & explicit_only) &&
           !has_named_experiment(experiments, f->name))
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.h b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.h
index 951d43c..2ca6672 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_debug.h
@@ -284,6 +284,13 @@ enum kk_experimental {
     * back through another resource over the same memory may be stale: must
     * be named, for measuring */
    KK_EXPERIMENTAL_BARRIER_DEVICE_VIS = 1ull << 21,
+   /* Playport (PLA-541): a fragment shader that needs quad helpers (an
+    * implicit-LOD sample, a derivative) does not get
+    * msl_disable_triangle_merge's fake barycentric read and select (or its
+    * sample mask write), so Metal may merge triangles into shared quads;
+    * derivatives along a seam may then mix two triangles. In the pipeline
+    * cache UUID. Must be named */
+   KK_EXPERIMENTAL_NO_QUAD_MERGE_BLOCK = 1ull << 22,
 };
 
 extern enum kk_experimental kk_mesa_experimental_flags;
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index 5687be2..c193084 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -1082,7 +1082,7 @@ kk_physical_device_init_pipeline_cache(struct kk_physical_device *pdev)
       kk_mesa_experimental_flags &
       (KK_EXPERIMENTAL_FP_PRECISE_ONLY | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_ROOT_TABLE_LOADS |
        KK_EXPERIMENTAL_UBO_UNBOUNDED | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_CONST_OFFSET_LOADS |
-       KK_EXPERIMENTAL_UBO_VEC4_BOUNDS);
+       KK_EXPERIMENTAL_UBO_VEC4_BOUNDS | KK_EXPERIMENTAL_NO_QUAD_MERGE_BLOCK);
    if (msl_experimental)
       _mesa_blake3_update(&blake3_ctx, &msl_experimental,
                           sizeof(msl_experimental));
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index 4b57074..7da02a6 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -749,7 +749,11 @@ kk_lower_fs(struct kk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir,
                             (pdev->info.gpu_apple_family == 7 ||
                              pdev->info.gpu_apple_family == 8) &&
                             state->ms && state->ms->rasterization_samples > 1;
-      if (!ms_bug_present)
+      /* Playport (PLA-541), MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=no_quad_merge_block: let
+       * Metal merge triangles into shared quads, as DXMT does; derivatives
+       * along a seam may mix two triangles (the pipeline cache UUID has the
+       * switch) */
+      if (!ms_bug_present && !KK_EXPERIMENTAL(NO_QUAD_MERGE_BLOCK))
          NIR_PASS(_, nir, msl_disable_triangle_merge);
    }
 
